**Bug:** The old implementation split on spaces and checked `hasPrefix("#")`. This missed tags embedded in larger tokens (e.g. `list,#urgent.` and `(#ideas)`).

**Fix:** Replaced space-splitting with a regex `#([^\s#]+)` that finds `#` followed by any non-space, non-`#` characters, then strips trailing punctuation (`.`, `)`, etc.) so `#urgent.` → `"urgent"` and `(#ideas)` → `"ideas"`.

**File changed:** `swift/Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift` (lines 4-8 → 4-23)

**Verified:** All existing tests (`"hello #world #swift"` → `["world", "swift"]`, `"just plain text"` → `[]`) plus the two reported cases (`"shopping list,#urgent."` → `["urgent"]`, `"(#ideas)"` → `["ideas"]`), plus order preservation and edge cases. Swift sandbox was blocked in this environment, so logic was verified via equivalent Python.


